{"id": "EUVD-2026-30540", "enisaUuid": "0e6ae35a-45cc-3504-b64c-3ea0973eecac", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nptrace: slightly saner 'get_dumpable()' logic\n\nThe 'dumpability' of a task is fundamentally about the memory image of\nthe task - the concept comes from whether it can core dump or not - and\nmakes no sense when you don't have an associated mm.\n\nAnd almost all users do in fact use it only for the case where the task\nhas a mm pointer.\n\nBut we have one odd special case: ptrace_may_access() uses 'dumpable' to\ncheck various other things entirely independently of the MM (typically\nexplicitly using flags like PTRACE_MODE_READ_FSCREDS).  Including for\nthreads that no longer have a VM (and maybe never did, like most kernel\nthreads).\n\nIt's not what this flag was designed for, but it is what it is.\n\nThe ptrace code does check that the uid/gid matches, so you do have to\nbe uid-0 to see kernel thread details, but this means that the\ntraditional \"drop capabilities\" model doesn't make any difference for\nthis all.\n\nMake it all make a *bit* more sense by saying that if you don't have a\nMM pointer, we'll use a cached \"last dumpability\" flag if the thread\never had a MM (it will be zero for kernel threads since it is never\nset), and require a proper CAP_SYS_PTRACE capability to override.", "datePublished": "2026-05-15T12:58:44", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T01:21:42", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/93d4ba49d18e3d7fb41a9927c2d0cca5e9dfefd6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/15b828a46f305ae9f05a7c16914b3ce273474205", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4709234fd1b95136ceb789f639b1e7ea5de1b181", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8f907d345bae8f4b3f004c5abc56bf2dfb851ea7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6e5b51e74a40d377bcd3081dd33fbaa0e1aa7e3d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2a93a4fac7b6051d3be7cd1b015fe7320cd0404d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/01363cb3fbd0238ffdeb09f53e9039c9edf8a730", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/31e62c2ebbfdc3fe3dbdf5e02c92a9dc67087a3a"], "aliases": ["GHSA-pm8f-4p6p-6x53", "CVE-2026-46333"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.97, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "00e9c553-a20f-3256-aff6-ad126f332c84", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.9.1 <4.10"}, {"id": "0a7a3097-bbc2-3efe-81c2-af1524046732", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e45692fa1aea06676449b63ef3c2b6e1e72b7578"}, {"id": "12090a44-c7a2-3e73-9337-bb250abd7c1a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.16.52 <3.17"}, {"id": "26864310-0a04-37ab-a3c1-430d2db3f482", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bfedb589252c01fa505ac9f6f2a3d5d68d707ef4 <01363cb3fbd0238ffdeb09f53e9039c9edf8a730"}, {"id": "3252bcf6-4bbf-353a-a2f5-fff7276e3d4d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.8.16 <4.9"}, {"id": "3483a0bf-dee1-3003-a41f-8483d9859935", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bfedb589252c01fa505ac9f6f2a3d5d68d707ef4 <6e5b51e74a40d377bcd3081dd33fbaa0e1aa7e3d"}, {"id": "35fbdb60-6cc4-3932-9e29-73e7acb1668b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.4.40 <4.5"}, {"id": "371387cd-7065-3f5f-a0a3-70c7b1dd9a07", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.139"}, {"id": "3b47d50c-20a0-3204-889c-82e91682bc91", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.10"}, {"id": "4a2bfdd7-bfe2-3b25-95f8-f69f1a6204da", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bfedb589252c01fa505ac9f6f2a3d5d68d707ef4 <15b828a46f305ae9f05a7c16914b3ce273474205"}, {"id": "4b870115-a9df-30bc-84a0-b201653bea77"